# Action Required: Prepare Your Mac for the Embedded Swift Workshop

Hello everyone! 👋

We're excited to welcome you to the **SwiftBengaluru – Embedded Swift Hands-on Workshop** on **Saturday, 24 October 2026, from 9:30 AM to 1:00 PM**.

This is a hands-on workshop where you'll write Swift code and run it on a **Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W**.

We'll provide the hardware kits, with two participants sharing each kit.

**Please complete the following setup on your Mac before attending.**

### 1. Hardware requirements

- Apple Silicon MacBook (M1, M2, M3, M4, M5, or newer)
- macOS with a compatible Xcode version
- At least 10 GB of free disk space recommended
- Administrator access to install developer tools
- Fully charged MacBook and charger

### 2. Install Xcode and Command Line Tools

Install Xcode from the Mac App Store.

Open Terminal and run:

```bash
xcode-select --install
```

Verify:

```bash
xcodebuild -version
clang --version
```

### 3. Install Homebrew

If you don't already have Homebrew, follow the installation instructions:

https://brew.sh/

Verify:

```bash
brew --version
```

### 4. Install CMake, Ninja and Git

Run:

```bash
brew install cmake ninja git
```

Verify:

```bash
cmake --version
ninja --version
git --version
```

### 5. Install Swift 6.4

Download and install the Swift 6.4 release toolchain for macOS from:

https://www.swift.org/install/

Make sure you select the Apple Silicon-compatible toolchain.

Verify the installed toolchain using its full path:

```bash
/Library/Developer/Toolchains/swift-6.4-RELEASE.xctoolchain/usr/bin/swiftc --version
```

If your installation uses a different toolchain name or location, adjust the path accordingly.

### 6. Install ARM GNU Toolchain

Download the macOS Apple Silicon version of the Arm GNU Toolchain for `arm-none-eabi`:

https://developer.arm.com/downloads/-/arm-gnu-toolchain-downloads

Our tested setup uses Arm GNU Toolchain 15.3.

Verify after installation:

```bash
arm-none-eabi-gcc --version
```

If the command is not found, the toolchain's `bin` directory needs to be added to your `PATH`.

### 7. Verify your setup

Open Terminal and run:

```bash
swiftc --version
cmake --version
ninja --version
arm-none-eabi-gcc --version
git --version
```

Note: `swiftc --version` may show your default Xcode Swift version rather than Swift 6.4. The workshop project will use the installed Swift 6.4 toolchain explicitly.

### 8. Important reminders

- Please complete the installation **before 24 October**.
- Bring your MacBook and charger.
- Bring a USB-C to Micro-USB **data cable** if you have one. We'll also arrange cables for the shared hardware kits.
- We will share the workshop starter project and final verification instructions separately.
- If you face installation issues, please reach out before the workshop.

**The goal is simple: arrive with your Mac ready so we can spend our time building real embedded projects using Swift!**

See you at the workshop!

**Team SwiftBengaluru**  
https://swiftbengaluru.org/
